[0.000, "o", "\u001b[39;49m\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[H\u001b[2J\u001b[23;11H"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[37m\u001b[44mCards: \u001b[30m\u001b[47mA\u001b[37m\u001b[44m \u001b[30m\u001b[47m5\u001b[37m\u001b[44m \u001b[30m\u001b[47m8\u001b[37m\u001b[44m \u001b[30m\u001b[47mQ\u001b[37m\u001b[44m \u001b[30m\u001b[47mK\u001b[37m\u001b[44m\u001b[46X\u001b[23;73H38 cards in deck  \u001b[24;11H         \u001b[31m\u001b[47m5\u001b[37m\u001b[44m \u001b[31m\u001b[47m8\u001b[37m\u001b[44m\u001b[52X\u001b[24;75H"]
[0.000, "o", "I have 6 cards  \u001b[25;11H"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[80X\u001b[26d\u001b[80X\u001b[24;89H\u001b[39;49m\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[6;11HThis is the traditional children's card game \"Go Fish\". We each get\u001b[7;11Hseven cards, and the rest of the deck is kept to be drawn from later. The\u001b[8;11Hobject of the game is to collect \"books\", or all of the cards of a single\u001b[9;11H"]
[0.000, "o", "value. For example, getting four 2's would give you a \"book of 2's\".\u001b[11;11HWe take turns asking each other for cards, but you can only ask me for\u001b[12;11H"]
[0.000, "o", "a card value you already have. If I have any, I must give them to you,\u001b[13;11Hand you can keep asking. If you ask me for a card value I don't have,\u001b[14;11H"]
[0.000, "o", "then I'll tell you to \"Go Fish!\", which means that you draw a card from\u001b[15;11H"]
[0.000, "o", "the deck. If you draw the card you asked me for, you get to keep asking\u001b[16;11Hme for cards. If not, then it's my turn. The game stops when one of us\u001b[17;11H"]
[0.000, "o", "runs out of cards, and the winner is the one with the most books.\u001b[19;11H"]
[0.000, "o", "You ask for a card by typing its name (a234567891jqk), type x to quit,\u001b[21;11HYou get to start.\u001b[22;11H"]
